  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Performance: the debug pipe is no longer attached unconditionally, removing a ~2s stall from every run (test suites that paid it are roughly an order of magnitude faster). Set TESTFRAMEWORK_DEBUG_PIPE=on to force it, off to disable it.\nSecurity: the debug pipe client now uses CurrentUserOnly, and both the breakpoint wait and the pipe write are bounded so an unresponsive UI can no longer stall a run.\nRun isolation: an artifact reference is now copied per run, so two runs of one timeline no longer share pinned state. A frozen run is now genuinely immutable.\nFixes: VariableReference.Transform no longer recurses into a StackOverflow; ConstVariable.Transform no longer drops an existing transform chain; FreezableCollection.Contains no longer throws once frozen; SequentialEvent honours cancellation instead of polling on; OutputRunDebugger is safe under parallel steps; a step timeout no longer leaves the abandoned attempt racing its own retry.\nUsability: reusing a run builder throws TimelineRunBuilderAlreadyUsedException instead of failing obscurely; immutable-variable enforcement is restored; logging no longer blocks the calling step.\nAlso adds PersistentEnvironmentContext.CreateAsync as a non-blocking alternative to the constructor, which is now obsolete.",
